  "system": {
    "category": "feature",
    "source": "Bad Eden (2024 rules)",
    "tags": [],
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>“You were never lucky. You were early.”</em></p><p><strong>The Horns Know (tier uses / Soma Break).</strong> Bad luck is just the future arriving before the paperwork. When a creature you can see within 12 squares makes an attack roll, a check, or a defense check, you can use your reaction to decide it already happened the other way: the roll rerolls its lowest die or is Imposed (your choice), and you can do this after the dice are rolled but before the GM says whether it succeeds.</p><p><strong>Crossroads Kin.</strong> When you use Crossroads Hare, you can bring one willing creature within 1 square of you along, and you both arrive at 1 Integrity with one level of Strain. The token you leave behind is now two tokens, and the story gets a second hare.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
